# Computer3 & Mainframe2 Architectural Map

This document serves as the definitive architectural map and reference guide for Goonstation's `computer3` (Legacy ThinkDOS) and `mainframe2` (DWAINE OS / TermOS) codebase. It establishes clear system boundaries, documents directory hierarchies, and details the data flow and execution lifecycle across both operating system environments.

---

## 1. High-Level Architectural Overview

Goonstation's computing simulation is divided into two distinct, coexisting architectural generations. Understanding the boundary between these two systems is critical for debugging, writing programs, or interfacing with hardware.

| Feature / Dimension | Legacy Computer3 (`computer3/`) | Modern Mainframe2 (`mainframe2/`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Primary Hardware** | `/obj/machinery/computer3` (Standalone Terminals) | `/obj/machinery/networked/mainframe` (Centralized Mainframes) |
| **Operating System** | **ThinkDOS** (`base_os.dm`) | **DWAINE OS / TermOS** (`kernel.dm`, `shell.dm`) |
| **Base Program Datum**| `/datum/computer/file/terminal_program` | `/datum/computer/file/mainframe_program` |
| **Hardware Interfacing**| Direct peripheral cards (`/obj/item/peripheral`) | PNET Wirenets & Device Drivers (`os_drivers.dm`) |
| **Execution Model** | Single active program + background processing loop | Multi-process Kernel scheduling, forking, and IPC |
| **User Interface** | Popup HTML windows (`updateUsrDialog()`) | Stream-based terminal buffers (`DWAINE_COMMAND_*`) |
| **Storage Medium** | Floppy Disks (`disks.dm`) & Fixed HDDs (`harddrives.dm`) | Memcards (`mainframe2.dm`) & Tape Drives (`tapes.dm`) |

---

## 2. Directory & File Hierarchy Map

```
